<p>New genetic research suggests dogs were living alongside humans about 16,000 years ago — roughly 5,000 years earlier than the previous earliest genetic evidence for domesticated dogs. The findings suggest dogs accompanied hunter-gatherer groups well before farming emerged, strengthening the case that the human-dog relationship began in the late Ice Age. To trace those early origins and follow how dog populations spread with people, researchers analyzed ancient DNA from dog and wolf remains.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/Hssokf24L0o9pR_si99Q7_JCZckTMwDBBKiH4Fq73kIg1ij3XRKhSpz0mnBQcN-6luNk5rh78awCgRlom3NuR1Bp5p14-TsSgIqQKGrjzOUFyCt-_Ks2kl_ymakInVo6k0T5Z2KL_XDgcXWQkMOz3l-jiCXM2qKHb-F8V2ITorVP4ZWo5H3Ij9hebqArf_sgC8uxETbK7HoRu60ts4omyiFBuIY_-cE34gcwxv8Sfs_LbIcGGsH-eP6pdlpOAwvZxrek1F8RPbaWeKVTPA' alt='FILE - Four dachshunds wait in a basket of a breeder at a dog show in Dortmund, Germany, Friday, Nov. 8, 2024. (AP Photo/Martin Meissner, file)' /><br /><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Deutsche Welle framed the findings around dogs serving as companions and guardians even before the last Ice Age ended. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/humans-and-dogs-scientists-find-new-proof-of-ancient-bond/a-76533203'>Deutsche Welle</a>)</li><li>The New York Times emphasized that dog lineages may have spread through exchanges among hunter-gatherer groups, pointing to prehistoric social networks rather than a simple one-origin story. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/25/science/paleontology-humans-dogs-dna.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>The Globe and Mail highlighted how ancient DNA is helping researchers tackle two open questions at once: what the earliest dogs looked like and where they came from. (<a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-dog-genes-origins-scientific-study/'>The Globe and Mail</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/oldest-dog-dna-suggests-16000-years-of-human-companionship'>Oldest dog DNA suggests 16,000 years of human companionship</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/humans-and-dogs-scientists-find-new-proof-of-ancient-bond/a-76533203'>Humans and dogs — scientists find new proof of ancient bond</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-dog-genes-origins-scientific-study/'>Ancient dog DNA reveals new secrets about our furry companions’ origins</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/25/science/paleontology-humans-dogs-dna.html'>Humans Had Dogs Before They Had Farming, Ancient DNA Confirms</a> - nytimes.com</li></ul>